/**

@page page_exahype2_time_step One time step

\tableofcontents

`Derived` names the generated solver class of `Solver.h.jinja2`.
The solver families call the static methods of `Derived` as the PDE terms.
A solver family calls a PDE term only when `Derived` defines it.
The concepts of exahype2::terms, such as exahype2::terms::HasFlux, test which PDE terms `Derived` defines.
The constants of `Derived` select the branches below.
Every functor below, such as exahype2::fv::singlestep::UpdatePatches, runs through tarch::accelerator::parallelFor() or tarch::accelerator::parallelReduce() with one work item per cell, face, level jump or particle.
The host backend runs the work items on the OpenMP threads of the rank.
A GPU backend runs the work items on the device.
A cell, face or level jump of peano4::Adjacency::Local reads only data of its own rank.
It runs while the MPI messages of peano4::HaloExchange travel.

# From the runner to the solver family

Every rank runs exahype2::runner::Runner::runTimeLoop().
The loop decides every step from reduced values only.
Every rank then runs the same steps.

1. exahype2::runner::Runner::runTimeLoop(), once per step:
   1. exahype2::runner::Runner::applyMeshUpdates() runs the regrid when exahype2::runner::Runner::hasPendingMeshUpdates() returns true.
   2. exahype2::runner::Runner::runStep() runs a plot or a time step.
2. exahype2::runner::Runner::runStep():
   1. exahype2::runner::Runner::executeStep() calls the `performTimeStep` entry of exahype2::runner::SolverRepositoryCallbacks.
   2. exahype2::runner::Runner::finishStep() reduces the statistics and the values of the solvers across the ranks in one tarch::mpi::ReductionRecord.
3. The generated `createRepositoryCallbacks()` of `Main.cpp.jinja2` binds this entry to the generated `performTimeStep()` of `SolverRepository.cpp.jinja2`.
4. The generated `performTimeStep()` calls exahype2::SolverRepository::performTimeStep() with peano4::Spacetree::getCellConnectivity().
5. exahype2::SolverRepository::performTimeStep():
   1. exahype2::RefinementRequests::clear() resets the votes.
   2. `performTimeStep()` of every solver runs in the order of the repository's constructor arguments.
   3. exahype2::SolverRepository::commitRefinementRequests() gathers the votes of all ranks through exahype2::RefinementRequests::getRefinementRequests() and MPI allgather.
6. The generated solver base class of `SolverBase.cpp.jinja2` defines `performTimeStep()` for a solver with tracers or with code from `on_start_time_step()` or `on_finish_time_step()`:
   1. The code of `on_start_time_step()` runs.
   2. `SolverFamily::performTimeStep()` runs the solver family.
   3. `traceTracers()` moves the tracers.
   4. The code of `on_finish_time_step()` runs.
7. For every other solver, exahype2::SolverRepository::performTimeStep() calls the solver family directly.

# Finite volumes

exahype2::fv::Solver::performTimeStep():

1. exahype2::TimeStepping::startTimeStep() returns the time step size.
2. peano4::HaloExchange::post() sends the own halves of the exchanged faces to the neighbour ranks with MPI.
3. exahype2::fv::Solver::applyBoundaryConditions() runs exahype2::fv::ApplyBoundaryConditions on the boundary faces.
4. exahype2::fv::Patch::applyBoundaryConditions() calls `Derived::boundaryConditions()`.
5. exahype2::interpolateCoarseFaces() runs exahype2::fv::InterpolateHaloHalves on the local level jumps.
6. exahype2::fv::Solver::updatePatches() updates the patches of the local cells in place.
7. peano4::HaloExchange::wait() writes the halves of the neighbour ranks.
8. exahype2::interpolateCoarseFaces() runs on the remote level jumps.
9. exahype2::fv::Solver::updatePatches() updates the patches of the remote cells in place.
10. exahype2::fv::Solver::projectOntoFaces() copies the outer layers of every patch into its own face halves.
11. exahype2::restrictFineFaces() runs exahype2::fv::RestrictHaloHalves.
12. exahype2::TimeStepping::advanceTimeStamp() adds the time step size to the time stamp.
13. exahype2::fv::Solver::proposeTimeStepSize() raises the wave speed maximum of this rank or sets a fixed time step size.
14. exahype2::fv::Solver::measureError() records the error norms when a snapshot is due.
15. exahype2::RefinementVotes::voteOnEveryCell() calls `Derived::refinementCriterion()` in every time step but the first after a regrid.

exahype2::fv::Solver::updatePatches():

1. exahype2::fv::singlestep::UpdatePatches calls exahype2::fv::singlestep::PatchUpdate::computeVolumeUpdate() on every volume of every listed cell.
   The host runs it through exahype2::fv::singlestep::PatchUpdate::update().
   A device runs it with one thread per volume.
2. exahype2::fv::singlestep::SingleStep::applyToVolume() advances one volume as `Derived::TimeIntegration`:
   1. `Derived::sourceTerm()` adds the source.
   2. `Derived::Reconstruction::accumulateFluxDivergence()` adds the flux divergence.
   3. exahype2::fv::reconstruction::Constant::accumulateFluxDivergence() calls `Derived::diffusiveSourceTerm()`.
   4. exahype2::fv::reconstruction::LimitedLinear::evolveFaceStates() reads the slope from `Derived::limitedDifference()` or from a slope limiter such as exahype2::fv::limiter::Minmod::limitedDifference().
   5. With exahype2::terms::HasRiemannSolver, exahype2::fv::solveRiemannProblemOnVolumeFace() calls `Derived::solveRiemannProblem()`.
   6. Without exahype2::terms::HasRiemannSolver, a Rusanov flux calls `Derived::flux()`, `Derived::nonconservativeProduct()` and `Derived::maxEigenvalue()`.
3. `Derived::postprocessUpdatedPatch()` runs on the updated patch.
4. exahype2::fv::Patch::getMaxEigenvalueOfVolume() calls `Derived::maxEigenvalue()` on every updated volume under an adaptive rule.
5. tarch::accelerator::parallelReduce() reduces the wave speeds over the cells with exahype2::MaxEigenvalueReduction.

# Discontinuous Galerkin faces

exahype2::dg::ader::Solver and exahype2::dg::rk::Solver run the same face phase between their cell projection and their cell update:

1. The cell projection of the solver family runs on the remote cells.
2. peano4::HaloExchange::post() sends the own halves of the face states and of the face fluxes to the neighbour ranks with MPI.
3. The cell projection of the solver family runs on the local cells.
4. exahype2::interpolateCoarseFaces() runs exahype2::dg::InterpolateFaceHalves on the local level jumps.
5. exahype2::dg::Solver::solveRiemannProblems() runs on the local faces.
6. peano4::HaloExchange::wait() writes the halves of the neighbour ranks into both face pools.
7. exahype2::interpolateCoarseFaces() runs on the remote level jumps.
8. exahype2::dg::Solver::solveRiemannProblems() runs on the remote faces.
9. exahype2::restrictFineFaces() runs exahype2::dg::RestrictFluxHalves on the remote level jumps.
10. peano4::HaloExchange::post() sends the restricted face fluxes to the neighbour ranks.
11. exahype2::restrictFineFaces() runs on the local level jumps.
12. The cell update of the solver family runs on the local cells.
13. peano4::HaloExchange::wait() writes the face fluxes of the neighbour ranks.
14. The cell update of the solver family runs on the remote cells.

exahype2::dg::Solver::solveRiemannProblems():

1. exahype2::dg::SolveRiemannProblems calls exahype2::dg::solveRiemannProblemOnFace() on every face of the list.
2. exahype2::dg::applyBoundaryConditions() calls `Derived::boundaryConditions()` on a boundary face.
3. exahype2::dg::evaluateFluxOnFace() calls `Derived::flux()` on the outer half of a boundary face.
4. exahype2::dg::solveRiemannProblemOnHalves() branches:
   - With exahype2::terms::HasRiemannSolver, exahype2::dg::solveRiemannProblemOnHalves() calls `Derived::solveRiemannProblem()`.
   - With `Derived::IsLinear`, exahype2::dg::solveLinearRiemannProblem() calls `Derived::maxEigenvalue()`, `Derived::nonconservativeProduct()`, `Derived::multiplyMaterialParameterMatrix()` and `Derived::flux()`.
   - Otherwise, exahype2::dg::solveRiemannProblem() calls `Derived::maxEigenvalue()` and `Derived::nonconservativeProduct()`.
5. With a subcell limiter, exahype2::dg::SolveRiemannProblems also stores the numerical flux that each side applies in the pool of exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::getAppliedFluxes().

# ADER-DG

exahype2::dg::ader::Solver::performTimeStep():

1. exahype2::TimeStepping::startTimeStep() returns the time step size.
2. exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::openTimeStep() runs for a solver with a limiter.
3. The face phase runs with exahype2::dg::ader::Solver::predict() as the cell projection and exahype2::dg::ader::Solver::correct() as the cell update.
4. exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::closeTimeStep() returns the wave speeds of the step for a solver with a limiter.
5. exahype2::dg::Solver::closeTimeStep() advances the time stamp and raises the wave speed maxima of this rank or sets a fixed time step size.
6. exahype2::dg::Solver::measureError() records the error norms when a snapshot is due.
7. exahype2::dg::Solver::voteOnRefinement() votes in every time step but the first after a regrid:
   - A solver with a cell predicate calls exahype2::RefinementVotes::voteOnCells().
   - Every other solver calls exahype2::RefinementVotes::voteOnEveryCell().

exahype2::dg::ader::Solver::performTimeStep() branches for two solvers that exahype2::dg::ader::Solver::coupleWith() couples:

- The partner returns from exahype2::dg::ader::Solver::performTimeStep() at once.
- The solver that called exahype2::dg::ader::Solver::coupleWith() runs every call above for both solvers with the smaller of their two time step sizes.
- exahype2::dg::ader::Solver::copyFaceHalvesFromPartner() copies the halves of the coupling faces between the two solvers before every call of exahype2::dg::Solver::solveRiemannProblems().

exahype2::dg::ader::Solver::predict():

1. exahype2::dg::ader::Solver::predictCells() runs exahype2::dg::ader::PredictCells on every listed cell.
2. exahype2::dg::ader::Predictor::predict() branches on `Derived::IsLinear`.
3. For a linear `Derived`, exahype2::dg::ader::LinearPredictor::predict() builds the Taylor series of the solution in time:
   1. exahype2::dg::ader::LinearPredictor::evaluatePointSources() calls `Derived::pointSource()` before the first Taylor term.
   2. exahype2::dg::ader::LinearPredictor::evaluateFlux() calls `Derived::flux()` for every Taylor term.
   3. exahype2::dg::ader::LinearPredictor::addNonconservativeProduct() calls `Derived::nonconservativeProduct()` for every Taylor term.
   4. exahype2::dg::ader::LinearPredictor::applyMaterialParameterMatrix() calls `Derived::multiplyMaterialParameterMatrix()` for every Taylor term.
   5. exahype2::dg::ader::LinearPredictor::overwriteStateWithLinearSource() calls `Derived::sourceTerm()`.
4. For a nonlinear `Derived`, exahype2::dg::ader::NonlinearPredictor::predict() repeats Picard sweeps until the residual falls below `Derived::PicardResidualTolerance` or the sweeps reach their limit:
   1. exahype2::dg::ader::NonlinearPredictor::evaluateSpaceTimeFlux() calls `Derived::flux()`.
   2. exahype2::dg::ader::NonlinearPredictor::evaluateSpaceTimeSource() calls `Derived::sourceTerm()`, `Derived::diffusiveSourceTerm()` and `Derived::nonconservativeProduct()`.
   3. exahype2::dg::ader::NonlinearPredictor::solvePicardSystem() writes the residual of every node of the sweep.
   4. exahype2::dg::ader::NonlinearPredictor::averageStateOverTime() averages the space-time state over the time step after the last sweep.
5. Both predictors write the time-averaged face states and face fluxes into the own face halves with exahype2::dg::extrapolateNodalFieldToFaces().
6. exahype2::dg::ader::Predictor::subtractTimeAveragedVolumeIntegral() applies the time-averaged flux divergence and source to the solution.
7. exahype2::dg::ader::PredictCells marks the limiter status of a cell whose Picard iteration diverged.
8. Without a limiter, exahype2::dg::ader::Solver::predict() calls tarch::terminateWithError() on a diverged cell.

exahype2::dg::ader::Solver::correct():

1. exahype2::dg::ader::CorrectCells calls exahype2::dg::ader::Corrector::correctNode() on every node of the cells of the list.
2. exahype2::dg::addFaceIntegralsOfNode() adds the numerical fluxes of the faces to the node.
3. `Derived::postprocessUpdatedPatch()` runs on the updated cell.
4. exahype2::dg::getMaxEigenvaluesOfNode() calls `Derived::maxEigenvalue()` under an adaptive rule without a limiter.
5. tarch::accelerator::parallelReduce() reduces the wave speeds with exahype2::dg::MaxEigenvalueStatistics.

# Subcell limiter

exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::openTimeStep():

1. For a solver with observables of the discrete maximum principle, exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::reduceExtrema() runs in the first time step after the initialisation or a regrid:
   1. exahype2::dg::limiting::ReduceReferenceExtrema calls exahype2::dg::limiting::Detector::reduceExtrema() on the solution of every cell.
   2. exahype2::dg::limiting::Detector::reduceObservableExtrema() calls `Derived::mapDmpObservables()`.
2. exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::openStep() runs exahype2::dg::limiting::OpenStep on every cell.
3. exahype2::dg::limiting::OpenStep copies the solution of every cell into its previous solution and the reference extrema of the cell into its own face halves.
4. For a solver with observables of the discrete maximum principle, exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::mergeNeighbourExtrema() runs one round per axis:
   1. exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::exchangeFaces() sends the extrema halves to the neighbour ranks.
   2. exahype2::dg::limiting::MergeNeighbourExtrema merges the extrema of the face neighbours in every round but the last.

exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::closeTimeStep():

1. exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::judgeCandidates() runs exahype2::dg::limiting::JudgeCandidates on every cell:
   1. exahype2::dg::limiting::JudgeCandidates runs the last merge round on the reference extrema.
   2. A cell whose predictor diverged fails the test.
   3. exahype2::dg::limiting::Detector::isPhysicallyAdmissible() calls `Derived::isPhysicallyAdmissible()`.
   4. exahype2::dg::limiting::Detector::satisfiesMaximumPrinciple() compares the extrema of the candidate with the reference extrema.
   5. exahype2::dg::limiting::Detector::getRelaxationParameterOfObservable() calls `Derived::dmpRelaxationParameter()`.
2. exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::spreadStatuses() sends the status halves to the neighbour ranks.
3. exahype2::dg::limiting::SpreadStatuses marks the neighbours of a troubled cell.
4. exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::listCellsOnSubcellScheme() lists the marked cells.
5. exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::recompute() advances the marked cells on their subgrids.
6. For a solver with observables of the discrete maximum principle, exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::reduceExtrema() writes the reference extrema of the recomputed cells.
7. exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::addLocalValuesToGlobalReduction() adds the troubled cells of this rank to the reduction of the step.

exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::recompute():

1. exahype2::dg::limiting::ProjectSubgridsOntoFaces calls exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellScheme::projectSubgridOntoFaces() on every cell on the subcell scheme.
2. exahype2::dg::limiting::ApplySubgridBoundaryConditions calls `Derived::boundaryConditions()` on the boundary faces of those cells.
3. exahype2::dg::RestrictFluxHalves restricts the Galerkin fluxes of the fine faces of every level jump onto the coarse face.
4. The subcell family of the limiter, `SubcellFamily::advance()`, advances the recomputed cells on their subgrids while exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::exchangeFaces() sends the subgrid halo halves to the neighbour ranks:
   - exahype2::fv::singlestep::SubcellStep for Godunov and MUSCL-Hancock:
     1. exahype2::fv::singlestep::AdvanceSubgrids runs on the local cells while the halves travel, then on the remote cells.
     2. exahype2::fv::singlestep::SubcellStep::advanceSubgrid() runs exahype2::fv::singlestep::PatchUpdate::update() on the subgrid.
     3. exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellScheme::SubgridSolver calls the PDE terms of `Derived` and `Derived::solveSubcellRiemannProblem()` for that update.
     4. exahype2::fv::singlestep::SubcellStep::advanceSubgrid() repeats the step with `Derived::FallbackReconstruction` when `Derived::isPhysicallyAdmissible()` rejects a subcell.
     5. exahype2::fv::singlestep::SubcellStep::imposeAppliedFluxes() replaces, on a face with one recomputing side, the flux exahype2::fv::singlestep::PatchUpdate::computePatchFaceFlux() reports by the Galerkin flux of that side.
   - exahype2::fv::ader::SubcellStep for ADER-WENO, patch by patch:
     1. exahype2::fv::ader::PredictPatches predicts the local cells while the halves travel, then the remote cells.
     2. exahype2::fv::ader::SolveSubcellRiemannProblems solves the Riemann problems on the faces with two recomputing sides. On a face with one recomputing side, that side takes its Galerkin flux.
     3. exahype2::fv::ader::RestrictFluxHalves restricts the fluxes onto the coarse faces of the level jumps.
     4. exahype2::fv::ader::CorrectPatches corrects the recomputed cells.
5. exahype2::dg::limiting::ProjectRecomputedSubgrids runs on every recomputed cell:
   1. exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellScheme::projectSubcellsOntoNodes() writes the subgrid onto the nodes.
   2. exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellScheme::reduceMaxEigenvalues() calls `Derived::maxEigenvalue()` under an adaptive rule.

# Runge-Kutta DG

exahype2::dg::rk::Solver::performTimeStep():

1. exahype2::TimeStepping::startTimeStep() returns the time step size.
2. Every stage of the exahype2::dg::rk::ButcherTableau of `Derived::RungeKuttaOrder` runs the face phase with exahype2::dg::rk::Solver::openStage() as the cell projection and exahype2::dg::rk::Solver::addFaceIntegrals() as the cell update:
   1. exahype2::dg::rk::Solver::openStage() runs exahype2::dg::rk::OpenStage on the listed cells.
   2. exahype2::dg::rk::OpenStage calls exahype2::dg::rk::Stage::open().
   3. exahype2::dg::rk::Stage::combineEstimates() writes the stage state.
   4. exahype2::dg::rk::Stage::volumeIntegral() calls `Derived::flux()`, `Derived::nonconservativeProduct()` and `Derived::sourceTerm()`.
   5. exahype2::dg::rk::Stage::projectOntoFaces() writes the stage state and its flux into the own face halves.
3. exahype2::dg::rk::Solver::combineFinalState() runs exahype2::dg::rk::CombineStages on every cell.
4. exahype2::dg::rk::CombineStages calls exahype2::dg::rk::Stage::close().
5. exahype2::dg::rk::Stage::close() calls exahype2::dg::rk::Stage::combineEstimates() and exahype2::dg::finishCell().
6. exahype2::dg::finishCell() calls `Derived::postprocessUpdatedPatch()`.
7. exahype2::dg::reduceMaxEigenvalues() calls `Derived::maxEigenvalue()` under an adaptive rule.
8. exahype2::dg::Solver::closeTimeStep() advances the time stamp and raises the wave speed maxima of this rank or sets a fixed time step size.
9. exahype2::dg::Solver::measureError() records the error norms when a snapshot is due.
10. exahype2::dg::Solver::voteOnRefinement() votes as for ADER-DG.

# Time step size

Every solver owns its own exahype2::TimeStepping.
Every solver advances by its own time step size.
exahype2::TimeStepping starts with a time step size of zero.
The first time step of a run sets the size of the later ones.

1. exahype2::TimeStepping::startTimeStep() starts the step:
   - Under exahype2::TimeStepping::Rule::Adaptive, exahype2::TimeStepping::startTimeStep() takes the size that the reduction of the previous step admitted.
   - Under exahype2::TimeStepping::Rule::Fixed, exahype2::TimeStepping::startTimeStep() keeps the size.
2. exahype2::fv::Solver::performTimeStep() and exahype2::dg::Solver::closeTimeStep() end the step:
   1. exahype2::TimeStepping::advanceTimeStamp() adds the time step size to the time stamp.
   2. Under exahype2::TimeStepping::Rule::Adaptive, exahype2::TimeStepping::raiseMaxEigenvalue() stores the wave speed maximum of this rank.
   3. Under exahype2::TimeStepping::Rule::Adaptive, exahype2::TimeStepping::raiseMaxScaledEigenvalue() stores the scaled wave speed maximum of a DG solver.
   4. Under exahype2::TimeStepping::Rule::Fixed, exahype2::TimeStepping::setFixedTimeStepSize() stores the size from the reduced smallest mesh width.
3. exahype2::runner::Runner::finishStep() reduces the values of the step over the ranks:
   1. exahype2::TimeStepping::addLocalValuesToGlobalReduction() adds the mesh widths and the wave speed maxima of this rank to the tarch::mpi::ReductionRecord.
   2. exahype2::TimeStepping::readValuesFromGlobalReduction() reads the reduced values of all ranks.
   3. Under exahype2::TimeStepping::Rule::Adaptive, exahype2::fv::Solver::readValuesFromGlobalReduction() and exahype2::dg::Solver::readValuesFromGlobalReduction() compute the CFL size from the reduced wave speed maximum.
   4. exahype2::TimeStepping::setAdmissibleTimeStepSize() stores the smaller of the CFL size and the time left to the terminal time while the time stamp lies before the terminal time.
   5. Under exahype2::TimeStepping::Rule::Fixed, new mesh widths reset the size through exahype2::TimeStepping::setFixedTimeStepSize().

# Regrid between two time steps

exahype2::runner::Runner::runTimeLoop() calls exahype2::runner::Runner::applyMeshUpdates() before the next plot or time step when the votes of the last phase change the refinement plan.

1. exahype2::runner::Runner::hasPendingMeshUpdates() calls peano4::Spacetree::requestsChangePlan().
2. exahype2::runner::Runner::applyMeshUpdates() repeats exahype2::runner::Runner::runMeshUpdateStep() while the votes change the plan.
3. exahype2::runner::Runner::runMeshUpdateStep() calls exahype2::runner::Runner::runStep() with exahype2::runner::Runner::Step::DynamicAMR.
4. exahype2::runner::Runner::regrid() calls peano4::Spacetree::regrid().
5. peano4::Spacetree::regrid() applies the requests to the refinement plan.
6. peano4::Spacetree::regrid() assigns blocks to other ranks when dynamic load balancing is on.
7. exahype2::runner::Runner::regrid() calls the `regrid` entry of exahype2::runner::SolverRepositoryCallbacks when the grid changed.
8. The generated `regrid()` calls exahype2::SolverRepository::regrid().
9. exahype2::SolverRepository::regrid() calls `regrid()` of every solver.
10. exahype2::SolverRepository::commitRefinementRequests() gathers the votes of the created cells for the next sweep.
11. exahype2::SolverRepository::deleteEraseRequestsOfRepeatedRefinements() deletes the erase request of every cell that the regrid refines for the second time.
12. exahype2::runner::Runner::regrid() calls peano4::Spacetree::finishRegrid().
13. peano4::Spacetree::finishRegrid() adds the freed slots to the free list.

exahype2::fv::Solver::regrid():

1. peano4::MigrationExchange::migrate() fills the new slots with exahype2::fv::PatchTransfer from the parent, the children or another rank.
2. peano4::HaloExchange::rebuild() lists the exchanged faces of the new cell connectivity.
3. exahype2::fv::Solver::projectOntoFaces() and exahype2::restrictFineFaces() fill the new faces.
4. exahype2::fv::Solver::measureMeshWidths() passes the mesh widths of the new grid to the time stepping.
5. Under an adaptive rule, exahype2::TimeStepping::raiseMaxEigenvalue() stores exahype2::fv::Solver::measureMaxEigenvalue() when the next time step size is positive.
6. exahype2::RefinementVotes::voteOnCells() votes on the created cells.

exahype2::dg::Solver::regrid():

1. peano4::MigrationExchange::migrate() fills the new slots with exahype2::dg::CellTransfer from the parent, the children or another rank.
2. peano4::HaloExchange::rebuild() lists the exchanged faces of the face states and of the face fluxes.
3. exahype2::dg::Solver::measureMeshWidths() passes the mesh widths of the new grid to the time stepping.
4. Under an adaptive rule, exahype2::dg::MeasureNodeEigenvalues measures the wave speeds of the new grid when the next time step size is positive and the time stamp lies before the terminal time.
5. exahype2::RefinementVotes::voteOnCells() votes on the created cells.

exahype2::runner::Runner::finishStep() of the regrid step reduces the mesh widths and the wave speeds of the new grid across the ranks.
Under a fixed rule, exahype2::fv::Solver::readValuesFromGlobalReduction() and exahype2::dg::Solver::readValuesFromGlobalReduction() then reset the time step size to the new smallest mesh width.

exahype2::dg::ader::Solver::regrid() calls exahype2::dg::limiting::SubcellLimiter::regrid() before exahype2::dg::Solver::regrid().
exahype2::dg::rk::Solver::regrid() reserves the stage estimates after exahype2::dg::Solver::regrid().

# Plots and tracers

exahype2::runner::Runner::runTimeLoop() runs a plot step before a time step when exahype2::SolverRepository::getMinTimeStamp() or exahype2::SolverRepository::getMaxTimeStamp() reaches the next snapshot time or the number of completed time steps reaches the next snapshot step.
exahype2::runner::Runner::runTimeLoop() runs one more plot step after the last time step when exahype2::runner::RuntimeParameters::getNumberOfSnapshots() returns a positive count.

1. exahype2::runner::Runner::runStep() runs exahype2::runner::Runner::Step::PlotSolution.
2. The generated `plot()` calls exahype2::SolverRepository::plot().
3. exahype2::SolverRepository::plot() calls `plot()` of every solver.
4. exahype2::fv::Solver::plot() fills the halo, copies the solution and the halo to the host and calls exahype2::plotter::PatchPlotter::plotPatch() with the volume centres. exahype2::fv::singlestep::Solver::plot() and exahype2::fv::ader::Solver::plot() plot the reconstruction of a higher-order scheme instead.
5. exahype2::dg::Solver::plot() calls exahype2::plotter::PatchPlotter::plotPatch() with the polynomial at equidistant points and exahype2::dg::Solver::plotFaces().
6. exahype2::dg::ader::Solver::plot() adds the limiter statuses and the subcells for a solver with a limiter.
7. The generated `plot()` of a solver with tracers calls exahype2::plotter::ParticlePlotter::plot() for every tracer set.

The generated `traceTracers()` runs after `SolverFamily::performTimeStep()` with exahype2::TimeStepping::getTimeStepSizeOfLastStep():

1. exahype2::fv::traceParticles() moves the particles through the solution the step started from.
2. exahype2::dg::traceParticles() moves the particles through the updated solution.
3. exahype2::particles::ParticleSet::relocate() moves every particle to the rank whose cells contain its position.
4. exahype2::particles::recordSnapshots() records the trajectories of a tracer set with a trajectory database.
5. exahype2::particles::measurePositionErrors() records the position errors when a snapshot is due.

The generated `regrid()` of a solver with tracers calls exahype2::particles::ParticleSet::relocate() after the solver family regrid.
*/
